+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+Validation is absent today: `createTask`, `renameTask` and `addTag` in `task.ts` return plain values, and `list.ts` composes them. No existing `TodoErrorCode` fits bad input.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** one place for the rules; domain stays pure and never throws; rejected input leaves the list untouched.
+
+**Non-Goals:** validating `untag`, `find`, filters or `complete`; changing tag/title normalization; limiting the number of tags.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Add error code `invalid-input` to `result.ts` (rule: add a code only when none fits; `invalid-state` means a wrong task status).
+- Put validators (`validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag`) in `task.ts`, each returning `Result`. Title is validated after trimming; length is counted in characters of the trimmed string. `createTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag` return `Result<Task>` and validate first.
+- In `list.ts`, validation runs before the duplicate / not-found checks and before the id counter is incremented or `now()` is called, so a rejection has no side effect. `rename` validates the new title before `find`.
+- Alternative considered: validating in `list.ts` only; rejected because `task.ts` owns pure task logic.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Callers of `createTask` etc. break] → they are internal (not exported from `index.ts`); update list.ts and tests.
+- [Priority is typed, so TS callers rarely hit it] → check at runtime since screens pass raw input.
