+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks get in: blank or huge titles, unknown priorities, empty or spaced tags. The list should refuse them with a clear error instead of storing them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `add`, `rename` and `tag` reject invalid input with a new error code `invalid-input` and a message saying what is wrong:
+  - a title that is empty or only spaces, or longer than 120 characters (after trimming);
+  - a priority other than `low`, `normal` or `high`;
+  - a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+- A rejected operation changes nothing in the list.
+- `createTask`, `renameTask` and `addTag` in `task.ts` return a `Result` (internal, not exported from `src/index.ts`).
+- Add `invalid-input` to `TodoErrorCode`, since no existing code fits.
+
+Project rules touched: "Errors are returned as a Result in the domain" (validation returns `err`, never throws); "No wall clock or randomness" (untouched); "No new runtime dependency" (none added); TSDoc on exported functions (added for new ones). Public API: `src/index.ts` exports are unchanged in names, but `TodoErrorCode` (already re-exported) gains `'invalid-input'`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-input-validation`: which titles, priorities and tags the list accepts when adding, renaming or tagging, and how invalid input is reported.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/result.ts`, `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `test/list.test.ts`.
+- Callers of `add`, `rename`, `tag` may now get an `invalid-input` failure.
+- No new dependencies.
